#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# chi_square_distribution

#% text
# `chi_square_distribution(k)` is the chi-square distribution with `k > 0` degrees of freedom: the sum of the squares of `k` standard normal variables.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mean(chi_square_distribution(k))
#% output
#= k

#% cell
variance(chi_square_distribution(k))
#% output
#= 2*k

#% cell
cdf(chi_square_distribution(2), x)
#% output
#= piecewise([[1 - exp((-1/2)*x), x > 0]], 0)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The 95 % point with 3 degrees of freedom:

#% cell
n(quantile(chi_square_distribution(3), 0.95))
#% output
#= 7.814727903251178

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `gamma_distribution`, `student_t_distribution`, `quantile`
